#MOVEMENT

     ^
     k
  < h.l >
     j
     \/

w			-> next beggining of a word
e			-> next end of a word
b			-> previous beggining of a word
gg			-> start of file
G			-> end of file
zz			-> set cursor in the middle of the screen
0			-> jump to start of line
$			-> jumo to end of lin

Number + G	-> Go to line of number

#EDITING

i			-> insert before the cursor
a			-> inset after the cursor
o			-> newline under the current one
O			-> newline over the current one

u			-> undo
p			-> paste

this cmds allow for number + cmd
d			-> delete
y			-> copy

g-			-> return to previous undo
g+			-> advance to next undo

#FIND & REPLACE

/pattern			-> search for a pattern
n					-> advance forward looking for pattern
N					-> advance backwards looking for pattern
:noh				-> stop pattern

:%s/old/new/g		-> replace all the instances of old, with new
:%s/old/new/gc		->	replace all the instances of old, with new, with confirmation

#FILE NAVIGATION

:tabnew + file		-> open a new tab with the selected file
gt					-> go to the next_tab
number + gt			-> go to the indicated tab
:tabm + number		-> move current tab to pos of number, index of 0 
:tabc + number		-> close indicated tab
:tabo				-> close all but the current one
:Ex					-> open file browser
:qa					-> exit all tabs and windows

#FUGITIVE

:G					-> go into the fugitive menu, inside said menu:
				->'s' for adding
				->'u' for unstage
				->'U' for mass unstage
:G + cmd			 -> execute said vim cmd

#NERD TREE

o					-> open in current window
t					-> open in a new tab
T					-> open in a new tab in silence
ctrl-w w			-> change to the next window
:NErdtree			-> Launches/closes the nerd tree
m					-> Opens Menu
go					-> Open in current window and maintaing focus on nerdtree

#CUSTOM

jk				-> Esc
Ctrl + s		-> Save file
